<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - Kian Ho H1 net falls 39 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Kian Ho H1 net falls 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1.43  vs  2.36</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    1.10  vs  1.81</p>
<p>    Turnover				29.64  vs 35.11</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.02  vs  0.03</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.98  vs  0.59</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation    0.52  vs  0.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 2.04  vs  3.26</p>
<p>    Tax					0.63  vs  0.93</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.02  vs  0.02</p>
<p>Note - Kian Ho Bearings Ltd said profits were hit by lower sales in Indonesia, a slower than expected recovery in Singapore and a weakened Thai economy, combined with higher operating expenses.</p>
